 * This test covers the following acceptance criteria:
 *
 * 1. Admin can POST a manual positive adjustment event (awarding points) for an existing customer, referencing an existing loyalty tier.
 * 2. Admin can POST a manual negative adjustment event (deducting points) for the same customer.
 * 3. Each event is correctly recorded, with all output fields matching input (customer_id, tier_id, change_amount, reason).
 * 4. Attempting to POST with a disallowed reason value fails as expected (error).
 * 5. Attempting to POST with a nonexistent customer_id fails as expected (error).
 * 6. Attempting to POST with a nonexistent loyalty_tier_id fails as expected (error).
 *
 * Note: Admin authentication/authorization checks are out of scope unless explicit role-switch APIs are provided.
 *
 * Steps performed:
 * 1. Create user profile (customer) via POST /ai_ecommerce/userProfiles
 * 2. Create loyalty tier via POST /ai_ecommerce/loyaltyTiers
 * 3. POST (award) loyalty point manual adjustment - verify all relevant output fields
 * 4. POST (deduct) loyalty point manual adjustment - verify all relevant output fields
 * 5. POST with bad reason - verify validation error
 * 6. POST with invalid customer_id - verify error
 * 7. POST with invalid loyalty_tier_id - verify error
 */
export async function test_api_ai_ecommerce_loyaltyPoints_post_admin_adjustment(
